# Deferral

Deferral is exceptional. Be slow to postpone. A follow-up without a time is not a plan.

Do not ship a gap as "temporary", 「暫定」, 「今はやらない」, or "later issue" unless `docs/roadmap.md` already has a named row that owns the follow-up (ID, and an Issue once one exists), or the item is already listed under **Intentionally out of scope**.

The row names when the work happens. Status before Grill is `Set after Grill on #n`. Acceptance text stays on the Issue. Do not copy it onto the roadmap.

Do not postpone in a way that leaves one path optimized or supported and another path of the same capability not. That intermediate state is not made acceptable by a follow-up row (`.cursor/rules/scope.mdc`). Maintainability is the check on every deferral.

Do not recommend a gap because the slice is smaller or easier.

Do not grow **Intentionally out of scope** in the same change that notices a gap. Adding or removing a bullet is Grill → Issue. An ungrilled dump into that list is not a plan.

If there is no row and the item is not in that list:

- do the work in the current Issue, or
- add the row in the same change that introduces the gap: ID, title, Issue. If it is not grilled, status is `Set after Grill on #n`. Do not write the acceptance text on the roadmap. Do not invent the acceptance text in order to fill the row.

Forbidden:

- "Temporary until the next phase" when that phase's acceptance text does not name the split
- "File an issue later" with no roadmap ID
- Closing a phase while a temporary gap is still in the code
- One optimized path merged beside an unoptimized path of the same capability

When a row becomes `Done` or moves to **Intentionally out of scope**, search both design files, both READMEs, and `.cursor/rules/` for its title and keywords in the same change. Remove or update every sentence that still lists it as waiting work.

```text
# BAD — P5-1 done; §11 and hpc.mdc still say "wider SIMD stays on its roadmap row"
# GOOD — the same PR drops AVX-512 from §11, both READMEs, hpc.mdc, and scope.mdc
```

A question about whether something can wait is not consent to leave it unplanned (`.cursor/rules/consent.mdc`).
